    "UnifiedTheory/Clay/YangMills/WilsonSuccessiveCovariance.lean": "b4b72345eac4de1129d5b3a78d34ebde1ec962e662175ee58f2a5e5184b60402"
  },
  "scope": "Proves full-Schwartz contact subtraction for the actual covariance removed by one independent SU(2) Wilson block. The literal periodic kernel is retained globally: its cutoff error vanishes inside the pair ball by actual no-wrap geometry and has amplitude at most 16/a^8 everywhere. Weighted Schwartz tails give error<=C*a*R^4*p05(F)+16*weightedMoment_m(F)/(a^8*R^m). The explicit path a=(k+1)^-8,n=4*(k+1)^9,R=k+1,m=72 gives local rate (k+1)^-4 and full periodic-tail rate (k+1)^-8 for every coupling sequence. Actual kernel, degree-four diagonal contact and their difference are constructed as continuous linear functionals on the complete two-point Schwartz space. A single fixed continuous seminorm controls the entire removed remainder by p(F)/(k+1)^4, independently of coupling and independent block. Exact cell pairing binds the result to real physical full-minus-retained covariance, and separated limits transfer conditionally if such a limit is established. Separately proves exact two-step covariance decomposition, orthogonality and positive cumulative variance accounting under true successive induced Wilson laws, including exact retention of final-coordinate observables. Proves actual third/fourth total cumulance identities, including all mixed retained/noise covariance terms. These results do not bound retained correlations, identify a physical coupling, establish bracket signs, or construct a nonzero continuum theory.",
  "full_schwartz_repair": {
    "actual_kernel": "K_a(x,y)=a^-8 C_S(sample x,sample y), with C_S the original-law covariance actually removed by an independent link block.",
    "tail": "K_a minus its tube truncation is zero inside the pair radius-R ball when 2R+2a<n*a and has absolute value<=16/a^8 globally. The weighted tail includes all periodic copies and contributes 16*weightedMoment_m(F)/(a^8*R^m).",
    "local": "The same actual degree-four relative-coordinate diagonal contact contributes local error<=C0*a*R^4*p05(F), where C0=massConstant1*4^5/24.",
    "path": "Let x=k+1,a=x^-8,n=4x^9,R=x,m=72. The physical period is 4x, the no-wrap condition holds for k>=1, and errors are<=C0*p05(F)/x^4+16*weightedMoment72(F)/x^8. All choices are independent of the test.",
    "coupling": "The bounds allow every beta(k). The explicit beta_b(k)=8b log(k+1)=b log(1/a(k)) tends to infinity for b>0, but neither b nor this beta is identified as the physical tuning trajectory.",
    "continuous_dual": "The actual kernel pairing, contact4 and their difference are continuous complex-linear functionals on Schwartz(Spacetime x Spacetime,C). Contact4 is supported on the diagonal. Fixed-cutoff constants may diverge.",
    "uniform_control": "An explicit continuous real Schwartz seminorm p controls the full actual remainder by p(F)/(k+1)^4 for every k>=1, beta and independent block. This is a uniform bound for the removed remainder only, not for full or retained correlations.",
    "covariance_binding": "Exact finite-cell pairing gives a^-8 Cov_full-contact4=a^-8 Cov_retained+o(1) on every real Schwartz tensor, without compact support.",
    "separated": "Disjoint topological supports imply diagonal-disjoint tensor support, so actual full-minus-retained separated covariances tend to zero. If a separated full-covariance limit is proved, the actual retained covariance has that same limit; no limit existence or nonzero value follows automatically."
  },
  "successive_integration": {
    "identity": "Cov_0(F,G)=Gram_0(F-F1,G-G1)+Gram_1(F1-F2,G1-G2)+Cov_2(F2,G2), where the second Gram is evaluated under the first true induced law.",
    "orthogonality": "First and lifted second noises are orthogonal under the original law; their sum has Gram equal to the two removed forms. Diagonal forms are nonnegative and their sum is bounded by the original variance.",
    "wilson_binding": "Exact block coordinate assembly, true first/second marginal actions and true conditional responses bind all identities to the original compact-group Wilson law.",
    "obstruction": "An observable depending only on final retained coordinates is retained exactly. Elimination alone cannot strictly contract all observables. Nonexpansion against the original divergent rescaled variance does not establish a continuum bound.",
    "missing_estimates": "Later effective interactions require new locality, weighted kernel mass and summable remainder estimates; the original independent-block stencil and Haar comparison do not supply these automatically."
  },
  "higher_cumulants": {
    "notation": "m=E[F|outside],eta=F-m,v=E[eta^2|outside],t=E[eta^3|outside],k4=E[eta^4|outside]-3v^2; outer expectations and covariances use the exact retained marginal.",
    "third": "kappa3(F)=kappa3(m)+E[t]+3Cov(m,v).",
    "fourth": "kappa4(F)=kappa4(m)+E[k4]+4Cov(m,t)+3Var(v)+6Cov((m-EF)^2,v).",
    "scope": "These formulas are exact for actual compact-group Wilson blocks with continuous characters. They expose the missing mixed estimates; they establish neither signs nor uniform higher correlations. Microscopic excess moments do not control these mixed terms."
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Bound the actual retained interacting covariance after contact subtraction and prove a nonzero separated reflected signal and logarithmic bracket signs. The new uniform Schwartz seminorm bounds only the removed-noise remainder, not the full or retained covariance.",
    "Quantify locality and weighted kernel mass for the actual successive induced interactions, with summable contact-subtraction errors and a bound on the final retained covariance. Exact two-step covariance accounting is now proved, but the first independent-block finite stencil is not automatically inherited by later effective actions.",
    "Control the mixed retained/noise cumulants and higher partial-diagonal counterterms. Exact actual third/fourth cumulance formulas now expose the missing covariance terms; microscopic Gamma moments and deterministic quadratic subtraction do not bound them.",
    "Construct a compatible full correlation hierarchy and prove its reflection covariance, reflection positivity, translation covariance, locality and other field symmetries after all required subtractions. The new diagonal counterterms are continuous linear Schwartz functionals at each cutoff but no reflection covariance or full generating positivity of these position/block-dependent counterterms is asserted.",
    "Establish the physical coupling trajectory and a nonzero continuum normalization with relative physical transfer-energy control, all required field/domain/cyclicity/spectrum properties and every compact simple gauge group. All twelve full Clay requirements remain open."
  ],
